WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 5.1 · Internal Systems & Operations
What a system is: your organisational operating map

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A system is a repeatable way of doing necessary work: be clear on the process before you choose apps.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.133
An internal system is a repeatable way of doing necessary work. It brings together people, steps, information, decisions and sometimes software. Your operating map shows your main systems, their owners and how information moves between them.

4
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:29.133
How your systems connect

5
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:40.093
Strategy and planning: Objectives set the direction; a plan turns them into work and dates. For example: The bakery's plan lists the pilot's six months and who runs each shift.

6
00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:50.681
People and money: People deliver the work; money pays for it and must be tracked. For example: The bakery records every flour order and the hours each founder bakes.

7
00:00:50.681 --> 00:01:02.011
Controls and data: Policies and controls keep the work safe; data shows what happened. For example: The bakery logs fridge temperatures daily and checks hygiene before any bread goes to market.

8
00:01:02.011 --> 00:01:13.430
Learning: What you learn shapes the next plan, closing the loop. For example: Stall sales drop in August, so next year's plan bakes less that month.

9
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.430
Why map it

10
00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:19.363
1. A weakness in one system shows up in another.

11
00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:25.037
2. It shows where hand-offs are likely to fail, before they do.

12
00:01:25.037 --> 00:01:31.341
3. It stops you buying apps before you know the process.

13
00:01:31.741 --> 00:01:32.341
What it guides

14
00:01:32.341 --> 00:01:38.756
1. This module: each system in turn, starting with what to set up first.

15
00:01:38.756 --> 00:01:44.059
2. Your process owners, calendar and tools in the lessons ahead.

16
00:01:44.059 --> 00:01:50.733
3. Later modules, such as your budget and policies, which go deeper.

17
00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:51.733
What to avoid

18
00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:57.407
Choosing apps first, before the process and its owner are clear.

19
00:01:57.407 --> 00:02:02.711
Making the map look good instead of making it useful.

20
00:02:02.711 --> 00:02:09.015
Systems with no owner, so nobody notices when they fail.

21
00:02:09.615 --> 00:02:11.415
You list your first-year systems, owners and key hand-offs.

22
00:02:11.415 --> 00:02:15.415
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:16.915 --> 00:02:20.015
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
